From: Gentoo local configuration
Subject: [PATCH] install Wayland find modules required by remaining Qt/KDE clients

SonicDE 6.31.0 still ships these helpers but omits them from the install list.
Keep them available for consumers outside the X11-only desktop fork.
Reviewed against the upstream 6.31.0 find-modules/CMakeLists.txt.

--- a/find-modules/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/find-modules/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ install(FILES
     FindPoppler.cmake
     FindPulseAudio.cmake
     FindQHelpGenerator.cmake
+    FindQtWaylandScanner.cmake
     FindReuseTool.cmake
     FindSasl2.cmake
     FindSeccomp.cmake
@@ -37,6 +38,9 @@ install(FILES
     FindTaglib.cmake
     FindUDev.cmake
+    FindWayland.cmake
+    FindWaylandProtocols.cmake
+    FindWaylandScanner.cmake
     FindX11_XCB.cmake
     FindXCB.cmake

     DESTINATION ${FIND_MODULES_INSTALL_DIR}
